  "cleaning_log": [
    "Renamed columns to snake_case with units kept (e.g. 'Torque [Nm]' -> torque_nm).",
    "Type -> ordered category L < M < H (low, medium, high product quality).",
    "No missing values, so no imputation is needed. A median imputer still sits inside the model pipeline so it would be fitted on training data only if new data had gaps.",
    "No duplicate rows (ignoring the ID columns) and no repeated product IDs.",
    "udi and product_id are identifiers, not measurements; they are kept for tracing rows but never used as features (product_id's first letter only repeats Type).",
    "Label check: 9 failures have no mode flagged (labelled 'unknown'), and 18 rows have a mode flagged but machine_failure = 0. machine_failure is kept as the ground truth because it records whether the machine actually stopped.",
    "TWF/HDF/PWF/OSF/RNF describe HOW a failure happened, so they are only known after the event. They are excluded from the features (using them would be target leakage) and used only for error analysis.",
    "IQR outliers: rpm: 418, torque_nm: 69. They are physically possible readings and they are where failures concentrate, so they are kept; removing them would delete the signal."
  ],
